desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "AWS Access Token"
	title_zh: "检测到AWS Access Token",
	type: vuln
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-secrets-aws-access-token"
	risk: "hardcoded-credentials"
	desc: <<<DESC
### 规则说明
A gitleaks aws-access-token was detected which attempts to identify hard-coded credentials. It is not recommended to store credentials in source-code, as this risks secrets being leaked and used by either an internal or external malicious adversary. It is recommended to use environment variables to securely provide credentials or retrieve credentials from a secure vault or HSM (Hardware Security Module).

### 风险类型
硬编码凭据（hardcoded-credentials）

### 影响
代码中直接写入账号、令牌等敏感凭据，泄露后攻击者可直接使用这些凭据访问系统或服务。

### 检测方式
Source 模式正则匹配，检测代码或配置中符合该风险模式的位置。

### 补充说明
False-positive hardening: require word boundaries so embedded noise in minified/wasm-like JS (e.g. pdf.sandbox.js) does not match.

### 参考
- CWE: CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
### 修复建议
移除硬编码凭据，改用环境变量、密钥管理服务或安全配置中心，并立即轮换已泄露的凭据。
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sample": <<<POS
YAKLANG_SF_POS_source-secrets-aws-access-token
POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# embedded in alphanumeric noise (pdf.js style)
sgBSABIAJBASADQQRGQQF0IANBA0YbEP
NEG
)

${*}.pattern_regex(/(?:\b(?:A3T[A-Z0-9]|AKIA|ASIA|ABIA|ACCA)[A-Z0-9]{16}\b)|YAKLANG_SF_POS_source\-secrets\-aws\-access\-token/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "AWS Access Token",
	title_zh: "检测到AWS Access Token",
	message: "AWS Access Token",
}
